    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Leimbach railway station sits on the S4 line of the Zürich S-Bahn, linking the village directly to the city center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leimbach_(Z%C3%BCrich)"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A single historic monument, dating back to the 12th and 17th centuries, earned protection status in 1924 and is registered as a monument historique.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://missionfranceguichet.fr/en/tourism-culture-heritage-commune-leimbach-68"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Leimbach earned the “Commune à découvrir” label from the French Ministry of Culture, highlighting its cultural and natural heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://missionfranceguichet.fr/en/tourism-culture-heritage-commune-leimbach-68"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The village lies in the lower Sihl Valley, a scenic corridor that has shaped its development and landscape.",
